{
  "video": {
    "id": "YCeKtM6Hnmc",
    "title": "DNA Structure and Classic experiments, excerpt 2 | MIT 7.01SC Fundamentals of Biology",
    "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YCeKtM6Hnmc",
    "channel": "MIT OpenCourseWare",
    "duration": 420,
    "language": "en"
  },
  "segment_count": 139,
  "segments": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "start": 6.84,
      "end": 7.45,
      "duration": 0.61,
      "text": "INSTRUCTOR: Good morning."
    },
    {
      "index": 1,
      "start": 9.98,
      "end": 14.63,
      "duration": 4.65,
      "text": "So, anybody check The New York Times yesterday?"
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "start": 17.39,
      "end": 18.413,
      "duration": 1.023,
      "text": "What did you see?"
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "start": 18.413,
      "end": 19.663,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "AUDIENCE: [INAUDIBLE]"
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "start": 27.59,
      "end": 29.154,
      "duration": 1.564,
      "text": "INSTRUCTOR: People, what people?"
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "start": 29.154,
      "end": 31.05,
      "duration": 1.896,
      "text": "AUDIENCE: I can't remember their names."
    },
    {
      "index": 6,
      "start": 31.05,
      "end": 31.524,
      "duration": 0.474,
      "text": "[INAUDIBLE]"
    },
    {
      "index": 7,
      "start": 31.524,
      "end": 31.998,
      "duration": 0.474,
      "text": "INSTRUCTOR: [LAUGHS]"
    },
    {
      "index": 8,
      "start": 31.998,
      "end": 33.248,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "AUDIENCE: [INAUDIBLE]"
    },
    {
      "index": 9,
      "start": 35.316,
      "end": 36.75,
      "duration": 1.434,
      "text": "I can't remember their names."
    },
    {
      "index": 10,
      "start": 36.75,
      "end": 38.87,
      "duration": 2.12,
      "text": "INSTRUCTOR: Yeah, the Crick and Watson people."
    },
    {
      "index": 11,
      "start": 38.87,
      "end": 40.06,
      "duration": 1.19,
      "text": "AUDIENCE: [INAUDIBLE]."
    },
    {
      "index": 12,
      "start": 40.06,
      "end": 41.03,
      "duration": 0.97,
      "text": "INSTRUCTOR: Exactly."
    },
    {
      "index": 13,
      "start": 41.03,
      "end": 44.23,
      "duration": 3.2,
      "text": "So, perfect timing, The New York Times had an article in"
    },
    {
      "index": 14,
      "start": 44.23,
      "end": 47.57,
      "duration": 3.34,
      "text": "yesterday's paper."
    },
    {
      "index": 15,
      "start": 47.57,
      "end": 52.13,
      "duration": 4.56,
      "text": "Francis Crick's correspondence with Maurice Wilkins during"
    },
    {
      "index": 16,
      "start": 52.13,
      "end": 56.43,
      "duration": 4.3,
      "text": "the critical year when Crick and Watson went down and saw"
    },
    {
      "index": 17,
      "start": 56.43,
      "end": 58.1,
      "duration": 1.67,
      "text": "the X-ray crystallography."
    },
    {
      "index": 18,
      "start": 58.1,
      "end": 59.19,
      "duration": 1.09,
      "text": "By the way, I made a mistake."
    },
    {
      "index": 19,
      "start": 59.19,
      "end": 63.65,
      "duration": 4.46,
      "text": "I said that Rosalind Franklin showed it to Crick and Watson."
    },
    {
      "index": 20,
      "start": 63.65,
      "end": 66.795,
      "duration": 3.145,
      "text": "Actually it was Maurice Wilkins who showed it to Crick"
    },
    {
      "index": 21,
      "start": 66.795,
      "end": 69.33,
      "duration": 2.535,
      "text": "and Watson when Rosalind Franklin was away."
    },
    {
      "index": 22,
      "start": 69.33,
      "end": 73.38,
      "duration": 4.05,
      "text": "Which, was itself a slightly complicated thing to be doing"
    },
    {
      "index": 23,
      "start": 73.38,
      "end": 75.67,
      "duration": 2.29,
      "text": "because it was really Rosalind Franklin's work."
    },
    {
      "index": 24,
      "start": 75.67,
      "end": 78.2,
      "duration": 2.53,
      "text": "But in any case, there was correspondence, some heated"
    },
    {
      "index": 25,
      "start": 78.2,
      "end": 81.23,
      "duration": 3.03,
      "text": "correspondence that went back between Crick"
    },
    {
      "index": 26,
      "start": 81.23,
      "end": 84.9,
      "duration": 3.67,
      "text": "and Wilkins and others."
    },
    {
      "index": 27,
      "start": 84.9,
      "end": 89.02,
      "duration": 4.12,
      "text": "And it was believed that the correspondence had been lost,"
    },
    {
      "index": 28,
      "start": 89.02,
      "end": 90.86,
      "duration": 1.84,
      "text": "had been thrown out."
    },
    {
      "index": 29,
      "start": 90.86,
      "end": 94.69,
      "duration": 3.83,
      "text": "But in fact, it turns out that in the papers of Sydney"
    },
    {
      "index": 30,
      "start": 94.69,
      "end": 99.13,
      "duration": 4.44,
      "text": "Brenner, another great person of that period, Crick's"
    },
    {
      "index": 31,
      "start": 99.13,
      "end": 102.75,
      "duration": 3.62,
      "text": "correspondence had got misfiled in Sydney's files."
    },
    {
      "index": 32,
      "start": 102.75,
      "end": 105.45,
      "duration": 2.7,
      "text": "Sydney had donated his files to the Cold Spring Harbor"
    },
    {
      "index": 33,
      "start": 105.45,
      "end": 107.19,
      "duration": 1.74,
      "text": "Laboratory on Long Island."
    },
    {
      "index": 34,
      "start": 107.19,
      "end": 109.36,
      "duration": 2.17,
      "text": "And they went through the files in the past several"
    },
    {
      "index": 35,
      "start": 109.36,
      "end": 111.27,
      "duration": 1.91,
      "text": "months and found them."
    },
    {
      "index": 36,
      "start": 111.27,
      "end": 113.99,
      "duration": 2.72,
      "text": "So we actually now have, as The New York Times reported"
    },
    {
      "index": 37,
      "start": 113.99,
      "end": 119.34,
      "duration": 5.35,
      "text": "yesterday, the letters with Crick and Watson and Maurice"
    },
    {
      "index": 38,
      "start": 119.34,
      "end": 123.2,
      "duration": 3.86,
      "text": "Wilkins about just that period I was telling you about."
    },
    {
      "index": 39,
      "start": 123.2,
      "end": 126.15,
      "duration": 2.95,
      "text": "It doesn't radically change any of the story."
    },
    {
      "index": 40,
      "start": 126.15,
      "end": 128.28,
      "duration": 2.13,
      "text": "But it really shows you the attitude."
    },
    {
      "index": 41,
      "start": 128.28,
      "end": 130.389,
      "duration": 2.109,
      "text": "And if you read the New York Times article, you'll find all"
    },
    {
      "index": 42,
      "start": 130.389,
      "end": 133.55,
      "duration": 3.161,
      "text": "sorts of juicy quotes about the attitude back and forth"
    },
    {
      "index": 43,
      "start": 133.55,
      "end": 137.21,
      "duration": 3.66,
      "text": "there, including the first model Crick and Watson made"
    },
    {
      "index": 44,
      "start": 137.21,
      "end": 139.79,
      "duration": 2.58,
      "text": "where they totally screwed up because they had misunderstood"
    },
    {
      "index": 45,
      "start": 139.79,
      "end": 141.37,
      "duration": 1.58,
      "text": "some number."
    },
    {
      "index": 46,
      "start": 141.37,
      "end": 144.15,
      "duration": 2.78,
      "text": "Anyway, it's interesting stuff."
    },
    {
      "index": 47,
      "start": 144.15,
      "end": 147.82,
      "duration": 3.67,
      "text": "And the reason I bring up this history is because science is"
    },
    {
      "index": 48,
      "start": 147.82,
      "end": 149.34,
      "duration": 1.52,
      "text": "done by real people."
    },
    {
      "index": 49,
      "start": 149.34,
      "end": 150.92,
      "duration": 1.58,
      "text": "It's a business of passion."
    },
    {
      "index": 50,
      "start": 150.92,
      "end": 153.13,
      "duration": 2.21,
      "text": "It's a business of trying to-- you know --"
    },
    {
      "index": 51,
      "start": 153.13,
      "end": 154.56,
      "duration": 1.43,
      "text": "science is wonderful."
    },
    {
      "index": 52,
      "start": 154.56,
      "end": 155.72,
      "duration": 1.16,
      "text": "It's objective in a certain sense."
    },
    {
      "index": 53,
      "start": 155.72,
      "end": 158.346,
      "duration": 2.626,
      "text": "And it's also about convincing others."
    },
    {
      "index": 54,
      "start": 158.346,
      "end": 160.83,
      "duration": 2.484,
      "text": "You know, a scientific result doesn't mean anything unless"
    },
    {
      "index": 55,
      "start": 160.83,
      "end": 162.58,
      "duration": 1.75,
      "text": "you can convince the community."
    },
    {
      "index": 56,
      "start": 162.58,
      "end": 165.73,
      "duration": 3.15,
      "text": "So it's an inherently human activity to bring people's"
    },
    {
      "index": 57,
      "start": 165.73,
      "end": 168.24,
      "duration": 2.51,
      "text": "attention to things, make things clear."
    },
    {
      "index": 58,
      "start": 168.24,
      "end": 170.4,
      "duration": 2.16,
      "text": "Anyway, that was kind of cool."
    },
    {
      "index": 59,
      "start": 170.4,
      "end": 174.16,
      "duration": 3.76,
      "text": "I invite you all to go look at The Times article."
    },
    {
      "index": 60,
      "start": 174.16,
      "end": 177.49,
      "duration": 3.33,
      "text": "You don't realize how much work we have to go to in 7.01"
    },
    {
      "index": 61,
      "start": 177.49,
      "end": 179.99,
      "duration": 2.5,
      "text": "to arrange these things to come out just at the right"
    },
    {
      "index": 62,
      "start": 179.99,
      "end": 182.25,
      "duration": 2.26,
      "text": "time during our curriculum."
    },
    {
      "index": 63,
      "start": 182.25,
      "end": 186.07,
      "duration": 3.82,
      "text": "But we pay off The New York Times and they do our bidding."
    },
    {
      "index": 64,
      "start": 186.07,
      "end": 191.53,
      "duration": 5.46,
      "text": "So last time we were talking about--"
    },
    {
      "index": 65,
      "start": 191.53,
      "end": 196.81,
      "duration": 5.28,
      "text": "I want to briefly go back to the Semiconservative Model,"
    },
    {
      "index": 66,
      "start": 196.81,
      "end": 203.01,
      "duration": 6.2,
      "text": "which I ended with last time, of DNA replication, the work"
    },
    {
      "index": 67,
      "start": 203.01,
      "end": 206.11,
      "duration": 3.1,
      "text": "of Matt Meselson and Frank Stahl, these graduate students"
    },
    {
      "index": 68,
      "start": 206.11,
      "end": 207.3,
      "duration": 1.19,
      "text": "at Caltech."
    },
    {
      "index": 69,
      "start": 207.3,
      "end": 210.68,
      "duration": 3.38,
      "text": "So you remember, our DNA double helix immediately"
    },
    {
      "index": 70,
      "start": 210.68,
      "end": 214.52,
      "duration": 3.84,
      "text": "suggests the secret of life, the way that you copy"
    },
    {
      "index": 71,
      "start": 214.52,
      "end": 216.48,
      "duration": 1.96,
      "text": "information to daughter cells."
    },
    {
      "index": 72,
      "start": 216.48,
      "end": 220.21,
      "duration": 3.73,
      "text": "Each strand is a sufficient template for the other strand."
    },
    {
      "index": 73,
      "start": 220.21,
      "end": 226.83,
      "duration": 6.62,
      "text": "If you just unzipped them, each would be able to serve as"
    },
    {
      "index": 74,
      "start": 226.83,
      "end": 230.85,
      "duration": 4.02,
      "text": "a template for replication for the other strand."
    },
    {
      "index": 75,
      "start": 230.85,
      "end": 231.42,
      "duration": 0.57,
      "text": "Beautiful."
    },
    {
      "index": 76,
      "start": 231.42,
      "end": 235.42,
      "duration": 4.0,
      "text": "It's called Semiconservative because you've conserved."
    },
    {
      "index": 77,
      "start": 235.42,
      "end": 237.18,
      "duration": 1.76,
      "text": "You used one strand."
    },
    {
      "index": 78,
      "start": 237.18,
      "end": 239.3,
      "duration": 2.12,
      "text": "And you've made a new strand on the other."
    },
    {
      "index": 79,
      "start": 241.94,
      "end": 243.95,
      "duration": 2.01,
      "text": "It seems obvious, but we can't take things"
    },
    {
      "index": 80,
      "start": 243.95,
      "end": 245.19,
      "duration": 1.24,
      "text": "for obvious in science."
    },
    {
      "index": 81,
      "start": 245.19,
      "end": 248.8,
      "duration": 3.61,
      "text": "Because the alternative model, alternative, which we know"
    },
    {
      "index": 82,
      "start": 248.8,
      "end": 252.61,
      "duration": 3.81,
      "text": "today is of course wrong, is that somehow the cell comes"
    },
    {
      "index": 83,
      "start": 252.61,
      "end": 260.079,
      "duration": 7.469,
      "text": "along, feels this double helix as a template, and somehow"
    },
    {
      "index": 84,
      "start": 260.079,
      "end": 264.0,
      "duration": 3.921,
      "text": "builds two new strands that are the same"
    },
    {
      "index": 85,
      "start": 264.0,
      "end": 264.93,
      "duration": 0.93,
      "text": "as that double helix."
    },
    {
      "index": 86,
      "start": 264.93,
      "end": 267.93,
      "duration": 3.0,
      "text": "They build a new double helix with both strands being new."
    },
    {
      "index": 87,
      "start": 267.93,
      "end": 268.59,
      "duration": 0.66,
      "text": "That's nuts--"
    },
    {
      "index": 88,
      "start": 268.59,
      "end": 269.35,
      "duration": 0.76,
      "text": "why would you do it?"
    },
    {
      "index": 89,
      "start": 269.35,
      "end": 271.53,
      "duration": 2.18,
      "text": "It's so obvious you could use one strand as the"
    },
    {
      "index": 90,
      "start": 271.53,
      "end": 272.63,
      "duration": 1.1,
      "text": "template for the other."
    },
    {
      "index": 91,
      "start": 272.63,
      "end": 275.42,
      "duration": 2.79,
      "text": "But this is what Meselson and Stahl had to rule out."
    },
    {
      "index": 92,
      "start": 275.42,
      "end": 279.23,
      "duration": 3.81,
      "text": "They had to rule out that that double helix stayed intact,"
    },
    {
      "index": 93,
      "start": 279.23,
      "end": 281.98,
      "duration": 2.75,
      "text": "and maybe the cell sent some enzymes around to feel its"
    },
    {
      "index": 94,
      "start": 281.98,
      "end": 286.5,
      "duration": 4.52,
      "text": "shape and somehow construct another double helix like it."
    },
    {
      "index": 95,
      "start": 286.5,
      "end": 288.69,
      "duration": 2.19,
      "text": "That would be a non-conservative model."
    },
    {
      "index": 96,
      "start": 288.69,
      "end": 290.9,
      "duration": 2.21,
      "text": "You weren't using any old strands."
    },
    {
      "index": 97,
      "start": 290.9,
      "end": 292.37,
      "duration": 1.47,
      "text": "The two old strands stayed together."
    },
    {
      "index": 98,
      "start": 292.37,
      "end": 294.01,
      "duration": 1.64,
      "text": "And you made two new strands."
    },
    {
      "index": 99,
      "start": 294.01,
      "end": 296.81,
      "duration": 2.8,
      "text": "That's what they were trying to distinguish between, this"
    },
    {
      "index": 100,
      "start": 296.81,
      "end": 298.91,
      "duration": 2.1,
      "text": "semiconservative model or not."
    },
    {
      "index": 101,
      "start": 298.91,
      "end": 304.3,
      "duration": 5.39,
      "text": "So I just remind you that their really cool, cool idea--"
    },
    {
      "index": 102,
      "start": 304.3,
      "end": 308.65,
      "duration": 4.35,
      "text": "see, they couldn't use a radioactive tracer that was"
    },
    {
      "index": 103,
      "start": 308.65,
      "end": 311.14,
      "duration": 2.49,
      "text": "different on the new strand than the old strand in the"
    },
    {
      "index": 104,
      "start": 311.14,
      "end": 312.71,
      "duration": 1.57,
      "text": "conventional sense."
    },
    {
      "index": 105,
      "start": 312.71,
      "end": 315.73,
      "duration": 3.02,
      "text": "Because, of course, they're made out of the same atoms."
    },
    {
      "index": 106,
      "start": 315.73,
      "end": 320.86,
      "duration": 5.13,
      "text": "But what they did do, as we talked about last time, was"
    },
    {
      "index": 107,
      "start": 320.86,
      "end": 322.88,
      "duration": 2.02,
      "text": "they take the DNA."
    },
    {
      "index": 108,
      "start": 322.88,
      "end": 327.02,
      "duration": 4.14,
      "text": "They grow it up in heavy nitrogen."
    },
    {
      "index": 109,
      "start": 327.02,
      "end": 330.57,
      "duration": 3.55,
      "text": "They then shift the bacteria to light nitrogen."
    },
    {
      "index": 110,
      "start": 334.9,
      "end": 342.97,
      "duration": 8.07,
      "text": "And, if in fact the Semiconservative Model is"
    },
    {
      "index": 111,
      "start": 342.97,
      "end": 347.29,
      "duration": 4.32,
      "text": "right, then the new DNA after one generation of growth will"
    },
    {
      "index": 112,
      "start": 347.29,
      "end": 348.94,
      "duration": 1.65,
      "text": "have a lighter density."
    },
    {
      "index": 113,
      "start": 348.94,
      "end": 352.53,
      "duration": 3.59,
      "text": "Very simple, except that they had to go invent a way to"
    },
    {
      "index": 114,
      "start": 352.53,
      "end": 353.92,
      "duration": 1.39,
      "text": "measure density."
    },
    {
      "index": 115,
      "start": 353.92,
      "end": 357.25,
      "duration": 3.33,
      "text": "They had to invent this centrifugation process where"
    },
    {
      "index": 116,
      "start": 357.25,
      "end": 359.78,
      "duration": 2.53,
      "text": "they spin really, really, really, really hard."
    },
    {
      "index": 117,
      "start": 359.78,
      "end": 362.56,
      "duration": 2.78,
      "text": "And the salt gets a little denser here, and a little less"
    },
    {
      "index": 118,
      "start": 362.56,
      "end": 364.38,
      "duration": 1.82,
      "text": "dense here, and a little less dense here."
    },
    {
      "index": 119,
      "start": 364.38,
      "end": 366.43,
      "duration": 2.05,
      "text": "And it's not a very huge difference."
    },
    {
      "index": 120,
      "start": 366.43,
      "end": 369.88,
      "duration": 3.45,
      "text": "But if you know the density of DNA, and you arrange your salt"
    },
    {
      "index": 121,
      "start": 369.88,
      "end": 373.19,
      "duration": 3.31,
      "text": "concentration at just the right density, you can spin it"
    },
    {
      "index": 122,
      "start": 373.19,
      "end": 376.71,
      "duration": 3.52,
      "text": "really hard so that there's some gradient in"
    },
    {
      "index": 123,
      "start": 376.71,
      "end": 378.55,
      "duration": 1.84,
      "text": "density in the salt."
    },
    {
      "index": 124,
      "start": 378.55,
      "end": 383.74,
      "duration": 5.19,
      "text": "And the heavier stuff will band here."
    },
    {
      "index": 125,
      "start": 383.74,
      "end": 386.01,
      "duration": 2.27,
      "text": "The lighter stuff from one generation of"
    },
    {
      "index": 126,
      "start": 386.01,
      "end": 389.26,
      "duration": 3.25,
      "text": "growth will band there."
    },
    {
      "index": 127,
      "start": 389.26,
      "end": 395.42,
      "duration": 6.16,
      "text": "And normal DNA would band there."
    },
    {
      "index": 128,
      "start": 395.42,
      "end": 397.11,
      "duration": 1.69,
      "text": "And that's a pretty convincing proof."
